# PPPoE Load Balancer Examples
#
# This directory contains example configurations for the ng_pppoe_lb
# (PPPoE Load Balancer) netgraph node.
#
# For detailed documentation, see ng_pppoe_lb(4).

# Prerequisites
# -------------
# Before using these examples, ensure the required kernel modules are loaded:
#
#   kldload netgraph
#   kldload ng_ether
#   kldload ng_pppoe
#   kldload ng_pppoe_lb
#
# Or add to /boot/loader.conf:
#   netgraph_load="YES"
#   ng_ether_load="YES"
#   ng_pppoe_load="YES"
#   ng_pppoe_lb_load="YES"

# Files in this directory
# -----------------------
# basic_2workers		- Basic setup with 2 worker nodes
# basic_4workers		- Setup with 4 worker nodes (multi-core)
# governor_auto		- CPU governor enabled for auto-scaling
# monitor_example	- Example monitoring commands
# pppoe_lb_test.sh	- Comprehensive test script with auto-scaling
#
# Shell Completions
# -----------------
# Bash completions (for bash-completion port):
#   cp _ngctl_pppoe_lb /usr/local/etc/bash_completion.d/
#   cp _pppoed /usr/local/etc/bash_completion.d/
#   source /usr/local/etc/bash_completion.d/_ngctl_pppoe_lb
#   source /usr/local/etc/bash_completion.d/_pppoed
#
# Zsh completions (for zsh port):
#   cp _ngctl_pppoe_lb /usr/local/share/zsh/site-functions/_ngctl
#   cp _pppoed /usr/local/share/zsh/site-functions/_pppoed
#   # Add to ~/.zshrc:
#   fpath=(/usr/local/share/zsh/site-functions $fpath)
#   autoload -Uz _ngctl _pppoed
#
# Tcsh completions (FreeBSD default shell):
#   cp ngctl.completion ~/.cshrc
#   cp pppoed.completion ~/.cshrc
#   source ~/.cshrc

# Testing
# -------
# To test these configurations:
# 1. Load required kernel modules
# 2. Choose a configuration below
# 3. Review and modify interface names as needed
# 4. Run ngctl -f <config-file>
